<h2>Libraries</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://leafletjs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Leaflet</a> — BSD-2-Clause. Map library.</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/Esri/esri-leaflet" target="_blank" rel="noopener">esri-leaflet</a> — Apache-2.0. ArcGIS REST client for the NOAA/FEMA layers below.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.11ty.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Eleventy</a> — MIT. Static site generator.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Live data sources</h2>
<p>Loaded live from each source's own server, not stored in this project.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://explorer.adaptingtorisingtides.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BCDC Bay Shoreline Flood Explorer</a> — CC-BY-SA (via the Caltrans open data portal). Attribute Caltrans/BCDC; redistributed copies of the dataset must stay share-alike. Planning-level only — see <a href="https://explorer.adaptingtorisingtides.org/about/a-disclaimer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BCDC's disclaimer</a>.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.usgs.gov/centers/pcmsc/science/coastal-storm-modeling-system-cosmos" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USGS CoSMoS / Our Coast, Our Future</a> — U.S. public domain. Served via Point Blue Conservation Science.</li>
<li><a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/slr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NOAA Sea Level Rise Viewer</a> — U.S. public domain.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.fema.gov/flood-maps/national-flood-hazard-layer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FEMA National Flood Hazard Layer</a> — U.S. public domain.</li>
<li><a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/digitalcoast/tools/flood-exposure.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NOAA Coastal Flood Exposure Mapper</a> — U.S. public domain.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/nationalsurge/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NOAA/NWS/NHC National Storm Surge Risk Maps</a> — U.S. public domain.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap</a> — ODbL. Base map data (all basemaps).</li>
<li><a href="https://openfreemap.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenFreeMap</a> and <a href="https://openmaptiles.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenMapTiles</a> — free, keyless hosting of the default greyscale (Positron) vector basemap; style and code MIT, schema/design CC-BY 4.0.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.hotosm.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Humanitarian OpenStreetMap Team</a> style, hosted by <a href="https://openstreetmap.fr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap France</a> — optional Humanitarian basemap (light use).</li>
<li><a href="https://www.esri.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Esri World Imagery</a> — optional Satellite basemap, for visualization only, with Esri/Maxar attribution.</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/domoritz/leaflet-locatecontrol" target="_blank" rel="noopener">leaflet.locatecontrol</a> (MIT) — the "show my location" button; loaded from unpkg with SRI hashes.</li>
<li><a href="https://maplibre.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MapLibre GL JS</a> (BSD-3-Clause) and <a href="https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-leaflet" target="_blank" rel="noopener">maplibre-gl-leaflet</a> (ISC) — render the vector basemap; loaded from unpkg with SRI hashes.</li>
<li><a href="https://nominatim.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap Nominatim</a> — address search and geocoding.</li>
</ul>

<p>A condensed version of this list also appears on the map's own attribution strip.</p>

